    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0469" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg381"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-01-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 16, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. “N.”]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state to the Department
                    that Mr. Férère, the minister of foreign relations, has not yet replied to our
                    note that Department instructed me to send, in regard to the license tax.</p>
                <p>Our merchants are being pressed to pay this unjust tax, and when they refuse the
                    Government refuses to permit them to take their merchandise from the
                    custom-house.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
